# What does NOT get published to crunchysfx.com.
#
# `assets.directory: "."` in wrangler.jsonc publishes EVERY tracked file in the repo as a static
# asset — the Tauri sources, the release script, the desktop and itch notes, the editor config, this
# Worker's own source. None of it is secret, none of it belongs on the public site either. Added
# after the same file was written for CrunchyVFX and the omission here became obvious.
#
# The site is only: index.html, styles.css, presets.js, dsp.js, synth.js, the icons, og.png — and
# version.json, which the desktop app's update check FETCHES, so it must never be listed here.
#
# LOCAL RUNS NEED flatpak/ CLEANED FIRST. This file filters the asset list AFTER wrangler has walked
# the directory, so it does not stop the walk: `wrangler dev` here dies on
#   EACCES: permission denied, scandir 'flatpak/build-dir/var/run/containerd'
# because a flatpak-builder sandbox left an unreadable directory behind. Workers Builds is unaffected
# (it clones the repo, and flatpak/build-dir is gitignored) — this only bites local dev and local
# `wrangler deploy`. Remove flatpak/build-dir + flatpak/repo before running either.
*.md
tools/
scripts/
src-tauri/
flatpak/
dist/
dist-itch/
synth-export/
Screenshots/
.vscode/
.github/
.wrangler/
wrangler.jsonc
worker.js
.assetsignore
.gitignore
*.aseprite
*.crunchyfx

# The Cloudflare PAGES twin of worker.js. Inert on a Workers deploy, so it is dead weight here — but
# if this project is ever re-created as a Pages project, DELETE this line: Pages needs the file
# present to run it as a Pages Function.
functions/
